{"availability":"available","full":"antonsoo/logdelta","name":"logdelta","description":"Diff logs by meaning, not by bytes: masks variables, mines templates, and shows what's new in the failing run.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-24T10:41:00Z","updated":"2026-10-09T22:01:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://antonsoo.github.io/logdelta/","topics":["ci-cd","cli","devtools","drain","log-analysis","logging","observability","rust"],"demo":"https://antonsoo.github.io/logdelta/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.865Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.865Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.865Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.865Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Diff logs by meaning, not by bytes. See what's new in the failing run.","When a CI job or a deploy fails, the useful question is \"what happened in this run that didn't happen in the good one?\" Plain diff can't answer it: timestamps, PIDs, durations, UUIDs, ports, and line order all differ between any two runs, even two passing ones, so a byte-level diff of a 4,000-line CI log is 3,990 lines of noise. logdelta turns each line into a template by masking the variable parts, clusters the templates, and compares template distributions between a known-good baseline and the run you're investigating. Lines that are one event, such as a traceback or the steps a failed job…"],"features":["Exact JSON field watches (unreleased): --watch-field /http/status catches a","logdelta diff ... --target — reports templates that are NEW in","the target, GONE from it (present in every baseline), or significantly CHANGED in frequency, plus NEW VALUE findings for a same-frequency content flip at a low-cardinality position (see How it works) — each with counts,…","Blocks: findings whose lines sit together are one finding. A traceback is one NEW","block that shows its lines with their numbers (in a failing job of the pytest project, 77 lines that were 51 findings in 0.2); the steps a failed job skipped are one GONE block. A stack trace logged fifty times is still…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/logdelta/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"11e7a7af2bc9464d444a2ada242ca47ffb11eba24a3641e7e9e516c52df599ea","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.972Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.972Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Diff logs by meaning, not by bytes. See what's new in the failing run.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/logdelta/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"11e7a7af2bc9464d444a2ada242ca47ffb11eba24a3641e7e9e516c52df599ea","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/logdelta/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.973Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T22:01:31Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/antonsoo/logdelta/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:29.976Z","hash":"11e7a7af2bc9464d444a2ada242ca47ffb11eba24a3641e7e9e516c52df599ea","originalBytes":40640,"storedBytes":40640,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["line","lines","one","template","baseline","new","target","value","logdelta","run","same","test","every","diff","log","each","first","two","only","block","json","templates","when","browser","docs","examples","findings","per","runs","position","which","logs","see","what","counts","failed","gone","source","count","known","masking","never","against","engine","field","report","values","build","cargo","npm","real","token","baselines","changed","checkout","input","last","numbers","page","seen","they","web","whose","across","any","before","between","blocks","divide","finding","http","key","like","once","own","still","text","word","words","bare","both","changes","cli","cluster","drain","example","file","gets","how","job","least","name","passing","shows","thos